From: fellows/ritik-b — "Visual Question Answering, Blind?" (2026-09-06)
Subject: [PATCH] register the VQA scenes, and fix two 9:16 toolkit scenes

Apply from the brutalist.art repo root, AFTER copying remotion/scenes/Vqa*.tsx into
runtime/remotion/src/scenes/:

    git apply patches/brutalist-toolkit.patch

Three changes, in order of how much they matter to anyone other than this reel:

1. scenes/ClaudeVerdictArtifact916.tsx — RENDER `sourceNote`. The portrait verdict
   component declared the prop (it shares claudeVerdictArtifactSchema) but never
   destructured or rendered it, so ANY 9:16 verdict beat silently dropped its citation.
   That is a "no source, no verdict" failure in the toolkit, not in a reel. Rendered with
   the same treatment as the 16:9 component: hairline rule, mono, staggered in after the
   last line. An empty string still omits the block, so reels predating this are
   unchanged. The matching `sourceNote: ''` default is added to BOTH verdict
   registrations in Root.tsx — its absence was also causing 2 standing tsc errors.

2. scenes/ClaudeTitleOutro916.tsx — size the portrait outro as a POSTER. It was failing
   GATE V's 55% canvas-fill floor at 22% (a ~106px title on a 1920-tall canvas). Also
   fixes a latent box-model bug: `maxWidth: 1080 - PAD_X*2` combined with
   `padding: 0 PAD_X` under content-box sizing left the title an 864px content box, so a
   long unbreakable word overflowed through the title-safe edge instead of wrapping. Now
   border-box with width = SAFE916.w, ~154px type, and the fill taken from leading and
   gaps rather than glyph width.

3. Root.tsx — register the 14 Vqa compositions. Each of the seven scenes is registered
   TWICE, at 1920x1080 and 1080x1920, from ONE responsive component: the title-safe box is
   1728x972 landscape and 972x1728 portrait, so the SHORT axis is 972 in both, one px type
   scale reads identically, and only the layout direction flips inside the component (see
   scenes/VqaKit.tsx). calculateMetadata turns the `durationS` prop into durationInFrames
   so a beat re-times to its measured narration instead of animating early and
   freeze-holding the tail.

Changes 1 and 2 are worth upstreaming on their own; change 3 is this reel's registration.

